        "description": "Impaired antibody response to polysaccharide vaccines",
        "category": "supportive",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      }
    ],
    "minimumForDiagnosis": "Presence of low IgG subclass levels with recurrent infections; supportive criteria such as normal total IgG and poor vaccine response strengthen diagnosis",
    "notes": "Diagnosis requires exclusion of other causes of immunodeficiency and consideration of clinical context."
